# What a published source tarball leaves out (~/openhamshack-nb/tools/
# source-site.py tarball, run for every release from 0.2.2, the first with
# a Windows installer). The repository is private; each release's tarball
# is public on https://source.brian-henderson.co.uk/#openhamshack-atv. Only
# notes that are internal and never needed to build anything go here: the
# GPL's corresponding source is everything needed to rebuild what is
# shipped, so a file the build, the tests or the packaging reads must never
# be listed.
#
# HANDOVER.md: the working notes passed between sessions - build and test
# hosts' addresses and accounts, the web host's folders, the radios on the
# home network. Nothing reads it; DESIGN.md and docs/ say everything about
# the program that it does.
HANDOVER.md export-ignore

# docs/screenshots: about 32 MB, more than the rest of the tree. Not source:
# ohsatv.ui.screenshots renders them from the simulator, and only
# tools/site-build.py reads them, for the site and the guide's web copy -
# neither the .deb nor the installer carries one.
docs/screenshots export-ignore
